; The ACTIVE conformance world for the joint Decomposition (@11.0) +
; ControlRatio (@12.0) port train (Checkpoint A campaign, issue #591 family;
; plan `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-17-decomposition-controlratio-port.md`;
; frozen source: `src/babylon/engine/systems/decomposition.py` (370 lines)
; + `src/babylon/engine/systems/control_ratio.py` (248 lines)).
;
; **Task 1 scope.** This file is the scenario ceremony ONLY — node/field
; declarations, no `decomposition/*`/`control-ratio/*` rule pack yet (that is
; Task 2 onward). It exists to (a) prove the scenario loads clean against
; both newly-registered systems via a load-smoke probe, (b) carry the
; frozen-mirror provenance for `decomposition_conformance.py`, and (c) host
; THE SPIKE (Step 5) that proves the two content-unprecedented query shapes
; §2 of the plan needs — both throwaway spike rules ran in a temporary Rust
; test, verified green, then deleted; verdict recorded at the bottom of this
; header. Later tasks in this train grow `content/rules/decomposition.bsl`
; and `content/rules/control-ratio.bsl` against this SAME scenario, chosen as
; the **fallback-trigger** world (`la-dying`'s wealth 400 < subsistence 500,
; the frozen `la_about_to_die` branch) so decomposition fires at tick 1 and a
; later single-tick golden is meaningful.
;
; **Enum order is a hash-bearing transcription of the frozen Python
; declaration order (ADR195)** — do not reorder:
;   `src/babylon/models/enums/social.py:34-41` — SocialRole (CORE_BOURGEOISIE
;   PERIPHERY_PROLETARIAT LABOR_ARISTOCRACY PETTY_BOURGEOISIE
;   LUMPENPROLETARIAT COMPRADOR_BOURGEOISIE INTERNAL_PROLETARIAT
;   CARCERAL_ENFORCER).
;
; **The carrier.** One `NodeType/INSTITUTION` node, `carceral-register` —
; the ONLY node of that type this scenario mints, so the driver's derived
; `CardinalityCeilings` gives it ceiling 1 automatically (plan §2), which is
; what makes `(select-max (nodes NodeType/INSTITUTION) 1)` a safe singleton
; accessor with no tiebreak to reason about.
;
; **`social-class/active` is an int 0/1 latch, not a bool field** — the
; established `social-class/active`/`organization/active` convention (no
; `bool` type token on the live `.bscn` deffield dialect,
; `scenario.rs::load_deffield`).
;
; **`social-class/organization` type — a DEVIATION from the plan's own
; default suggestion, recorded here.** The plan's Global Constraints table
; says "reuse the landed declaration — check `query-lane-e2e.bscn:57` FIRST",
; which declares `int extensive`. That declaration cannot seed this
; scenario's own `lumpen` vector (`organization = 0.2`, a fractional value):
; an `int` deffield's declared kind constrains SEEDING (class-surface
; amendment 1 — fractional seeds refuse at load; only a computed WRITE
; stores a fractional f64 verbatim), so a fractional literal in a `(node
; ...)` form refuses outright against an `int`-typed field. The OTHER landed
; declaration, `territory-conformance.bscn:104`'s `coefficient intensive`,
; both accepts the fractional seed and fits the frozen domain better: the
; frozen `control_ratio.py` compares `avg_organization` directly against
; `carceral/revolution-threshold` (itself `coefficient`, `0.5c`), so a
; coefficient-typed `organization` is the closer type match, not merely the
; one that happens to load. Used here; not a new type, still a landed
; precedent (territory-conformance.bscn's, not query-lane-e2e.bscn's).
;
; **No defaults (scenario.rs's own contract): every field every later rule
; will read is seeded on every node of its namespace.** Every SOCIAL_CLASS
; node below seeds all fifteen `social-class/*` fields (the eight
; frozen-input columns plus the seven published census-contribution fields,
; all zeroed pre-tick since no rule pack runs in Task 1); the one INSTITUTION
; node seeds all nineteen `institution/*` fields (the `persistent_data`
; state-machine transcription plus the published aggregates), every latch
; and aggregate zeroed.
;
; Five social classes, one carrier (declaration order fixes NodeId,
; `production-conformance.bscn:207-209`'s own precedent — never renumber
; when extending):
;
;   la-dying         LABOR_ARISTOCRACY, active, wealth 400 < subsistence 500
;                     — the frozen `la_about_to_die` FALLBACK TRIGGER vector
;                     (`decomposition.py:158-159`): makes a later single-tick
;                     golden fire `should_decompose = True` at tick 1 with no
;                     52-tick delay to wait out.
;   enforcer-seed    CARCERAL_ENFORCER, seeded INACTIVE with NON-ZERO
;                     population/wealth (20 / 100) — BLOCKER-1's seeding
;                     obligation (`add-node` is refused at content load,
;                     `structural_verbs.rs`'s `DEFERRED_SHAPE_VERBS`; the
;                     frozen engine's create-on-demand branch cannot port, so
;                     every conformance world seeds its own targets). The
;                     non-zero pre-seed is deliberate: a later `p04-enforcer-
;                     intake` rule's `(add ...)` mutation must be provable
;                     against a KNOWN non-zero baseline, not merely 0 -> N.
;   ip-seed          INTERNAL_PROLETARIAT, seeded INACTIVE with NON-ZERO
;                     population/wealth (77 / 33) — the OVERWRITE-provable
;                     twin: a later `p05-ip-intake` rule's `(set ...)`
;                     mutation must be provable against a KNOWN non-zero
;                     baseline that the write REPLACES, not accumulates.
;   lumpen           LUMPENPROLETARIAT, active, organization 0.2 — the
;                     ControlRatio prisoner census's SECOND role
;                     (`_PRISONER_ROLES = {INTERNAL_PROLETARIAT,
;                     LUMPENPROLETARIAT}`, `control_ratio.py:32-37`);
;                     untouched by the Decomposition pack (Pack A never
;                     reads/writes a LUMPENPROLETARIAT subject).
;   bourgeois        CORE_BOURGEOISIE, active — the non-participant vector:
;                     every published census-contribution field on this node
;                     must stay 0 through every later pack's tick (neither
;                     LA, CARCERAL_ENFORCER, INTERNAL_PROLETARIAT, nor
;                     LUMPENPROLETARIAT).
;   carceral-register INSTITUTION — the carrier; every latch seeded 0, every
;                     aggregate 0.
;
; **§2's eight `carceral/*` defconsts, all at shipped values**
; (`src/babylon/data/defines.yaml:293-300`) — `carceral/
; approaching-consumption-multiple` has NO defines backing (a bare `2`
; literal at `decomposition.py:155`; transcription note, not an escalation).
;
; **THE SPIKE VERDICT (Step 5, recorded here per the plan's own
; instruction).** Two throwaway spike rules were run through the real
; `run_once_into` driver against this exact scenario, then deleted (their
; `.rs` test bodies never landed):
;   (a) a carrier-anchored rule folding `(fold sum (nodes
;       NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS) (field-of it social-class/population))` —
;       LOADED AND EVALUATED CLEAN.
;   (b) a class-anchored rule reading `(field-of (select-max (nodes
;       NodeType/INSTITUTION) 1) institution/decomposition-complete)` —
;       LOADED AND EVALUATED CLEAN.
; Neither shape refused. The incidence-edge fallback design is NOT needed;
; Task 2 onward may rely on both shapes directly, exactly as plan §2
; specifies. Full command/output evidence: `decomposition_conformance.rs`'s
; own module doc comment and the Task 1 report.
(scenario decomposition/conformance
  (defvocabulary NodeType (SOCIAL_CLASS INSTITUTION))
  (defenum SocialRole (CORE_BOURGEOISIE PERIPHERY_PROLETARIAT LABOR_ARISTOCRACY PETTY_BOURGEOISIE LUMPENPROLETARIAT COMPRADOR_BOURGEOISIE INTERNAL_PROLETARIAT CARCERAL_ENFORCER))

  (deffield social-class/role enum SocialRole)
  (deffield social-class/active int extensive)
  (deffield social-class/population int extensive)
  (deffield social-class/wealth real extensive)
  (deffield social-class/subsistence-threshold real extensive)
  (deffield social-class/s-bio real extensive)
  (deffield social-class/s-class real extensive)
  (deffield social-class/organization coefficient intensive)
  (deffield social-class/la-census-population int extensive)
  (deffield social-class/la-census-wealth real extensive)
  (deffield social-class/la-approaching-flag int extensive)
  (deffield social-class/la-dying-flag int extensive)
  (deffield social-class/enforcer-census-population int extensive)
  (deffield social-class/prisoner-census-population int extensive)
  (deffield social-class/prisoner-census-org-weighted real extensive)

  (deffield institution/superwage-crisis-known int extensive)
  (deffield institution/superwage-crisis-tick int extensive)
  (deffield institution/decomposition-complete int extensive)
  (deffield institution/decomposition-fired-known int extensive)
  (deffield institution/decomposition-fire-tick int extensive)
  (deffield institution/control-crisis-emitted int extensive)
  (deffield institution/control-crisis-tick int extensive)
  (deffield institution/terminal-decision-emitted int extensive)
  (deffield institution/la-population int extensive)
  (deffield institution/la-wealth real extensive)
  (deffield institution/la-approaching-count int extensive)
  (deffield institution/la-dying-count int extensive)
  (deffield institution/enforcer-pop-gain int extensive)
  (deffield institution/enforcer-wealth-gain real extensive)
  (deffield institution/ip-population int extensive)
  (deffield institution/ip-wealth real extensive)
  (deffield institution/enforcer-population int extensive)
  (deffield institution/prisoner-population int extensive)
  (deffield institution/prisoner-org-weighted real extensive)

  ; CarceralDefines, src/babylon/data/defines.yaml:293-300.
  (defconst carceral/control-capacity 4)
  (defconst carceral/enforcer-fraction 0.15c)
  (defconst carceral/proletariat-fraction 0.85c)
  (defconst carceral/revolution-threshold 0.5c)
  (defconst carceral/decomposition-delay 52)
  (defconst carceral/control-ratio-delay 52)
  (defconst carceral/terminal-decision-delay 1)
  ; NO defines backing — a bare `2` literal at decomposition.py:155
  ; (`_APPROACHING_CONSUMPTION_MULTIPLE`-shaped constant, never named in
  ; CarceralDefines). Transcription note, not an escalation.
  (defconst carceral/approaching-consumption-multiple 2)

  (node la-dying NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS
    (social-class/role SocialRole/LABOR_ARISTOCRACY)
    (social-class/active 1)
    (social-class/population 1000)
    (social-class/wealth 400)
    (social-class/subsistence-threshold 500)
    (social-class/s-bio 5)
    (social-class/s-class 5)
    (social-class/organization 0.0c)
    (social-class/la-census-population 0)
    (social-class/la-census-wealth 0)
    (social-class/la-approaching-flag 0)
    (social-class/la-dying-flag 0)
    (social-class/enforcer-census-population 0)
    (social-class/prisoner-census-population 0)
    (social-class/prisoner-census-org-weighted 0))

  (node enforcer-seed NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS
    (social-class/role SocialRole/CARCERAL_ENFORCER)
    (social-class/active 0)
    (social-class/population 20)
    (social-class/wealth 100)
    (social-class/subsistence-threshold 0)
    (social-class/s-bio 0)
    (social-class/s-class 0)
    (social-class/organization 0.0c)
    (social-class/la-census-population 0)
    (social-class/la-census-wealth 0)
    (social-class/la-approaching-flag 0)
    (social-class/la-dying-flag 0)
    (social-class/enforcer-census-population 0)
    (social-class/prisoner-census-population 0)
    (social-class/prisoner-census-org-weighted 0))

  (node ip-seed NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS
    (social-class/role SocialRole/INTERNAL_PROLETARIAT)
    (social-class/active 0)
    (social-class/population 77)
    (social-class/wealth 33)
    (social-class/subsistence-threshold 0)
    (social-class/s-bio 0)
    (social-class/s-class 0)
    (social-class/organization 0.0c)
    (social-class/la-census-population 0)
    (social-class/la-census-wealth 0)
    (social-class/la-approaching-flag 0)
    (social-class/la-dying-flag 0)
    (social-class/enforcer-census-population 0)
    (social-class/prisoner-census-population 0)
    (social-class/prisoner-census-org-weighted 0))

  (node lumpen NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS
    (social-class/role SocialRole/LUMPENPROLETARIAT)
